From e02bd37448b111c86bb4447014f9c4db874666b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 371/488] soh: name the 29 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_nb.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 29 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Nb/z_en_nb.c.

  * func_80AB0FBC -> EnNb_TrackPlayerHead
    deduced, confidence HIGH: points Npc_TrackPoint at the player with
    NPC_TRACKING_HEAD_AND_TORSO

  * func_80AB1040 -> EnNb_TrackPlayerBody
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the same tracking call with
    NPC_TRACKING_FULL_BODY

  * func_80AB10C4 -> EnNb_ReturnHeadToNeutral
    deduced, confidence HIGH: eases the head and torso rotations back to
    zero

  * func_80AB11EC -> EnNb_SetupHiddenAfterCs
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drops to the invisible action with alpha,
    shadow and flag cleared

  * func_80AB1210 -> EnNb_WatchCutsceneEnd
    deduced, confidence HIGH: latches while a cutscene runs and, on its end,
    hides the NB_TYPE_DEMO02 Nabooru

  * func_80AB1284 -> EnNb_UpdateBgCheck
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs Actor_UpdateBgCheckInfo with Nabooru's
    dimensions

  * func_80AB1390 -> EnNb_IsCueAction
    deduced, confidence HIGH: true when the given cue channel is live and
    sitting on the caller's action id

  * func_80AB13D8 -> EnNb_IsNotCueAction
    deduced, confidence HIGH: true when that cue channel is live and on any
    action other than the caller's

  * func_80AB193C -> EnNb_ChamberIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the NB_CHAMBER_IDLE step: keeps the animation
    and eyes running and watches for the arm-raise cue

  * func_80AB19BC -> EnNb_RaisedArmTransition
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the NB_CHAMBER_RAISE_ARM_TRANSITION step: runs
    the animation out and watches for the medallion cue

  * func_80AB19FC -> EnNb_WaitDuringMedallion
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the step the enum calls NB_GIVE_MEDALLION,
    but its body only advances the animation and eyes; the medallion itself
    is handed over elsewhere

  * func_80AB23A8 -> EnNb_Kidnapped
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the NB_KIDNAPPED step: plays the cry and waits
    for the kidnap cutscene to move on

  * func_80AB2688 -> EnNb_ApplyRootMotion
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enables the animation's root motion and queues
    AnimationContext_SetMoveActor

  * func_80AB26C8 -> EnNb_SetupConfrontationHidden
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enters the confrontation action with nothing
    drawn

  * func_80AB26DC -> EnNb_SetupConfrontationKneel
    deduced, confidence HIGH: snaps to the cue's position and starts the
    collapse-to-kneeling animation with the kneeling draw mode

  * func_80AB2C18 -> EnNb_ConfrontationIdle
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the step the enum calls NB_ACTION_14: blinks,
    applies root motion and watches the cutscene; its purpose beyond waiting
    is not established

  * func_80AB2E70 -> EnNb_DrawKneel
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draw mode NB_DRAW_KNEEL: forces the wide-eye
    texture and draws the skeleton

  * func_80AB2FC0 -> EnNb_OverrideLimbDrawMouthOpen
    deduced, confidence HIGH: swaps the head limb for
    gNabooruHeadMouthOpenDL

  * func_80AB2FE4 -> EnNb_DrawLookDirection
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draw mode NB_DRAW_LOOK_DIRECTION: binds the
    current eye texture and draws with the open-mouth head override

  * func_80AB3428 -> EnNb_CreditsSit
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the NB_CREDITS_SIT step: runs the sitting
    animation and eyes while waiting on the credits cutscene

  * func_80AB359C -> EnNb_LerpAlongPath
    deduced, confidence HIGH: eases the actor from its recorded start
    position to its end position over the kREG-tunable movement window

  * func_80AB36DC -> EnNb_TurnAlongPath
    deduced, confidence HIGH: turns onto the path yaw at the start of that
    window and back onto the home yaw at its end

  * func_80AB3838 -> EnNb_OfferCrawlspaceTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: offers the crawlspace conversation, picking
    the line from INFTABLE_16C

  * func_80AB3A7C -> EnNb_CheckPathFinished
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops the walk animation until the movement
    window closes, then stands and idles

  * func_80AB3B04 -> EnNb_OfferTalkAfterPath
    deduced, confidence HIGH: offers the post-walk conversation, preferring
    any face reaction over text 0x6026

  * func_80AB3B7C -> EnNb_WaitForTextClose
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns to the idle action and drops targeting
    once the textbox closes

  * func_80AB3DB0 -> EnNb_IdleAfterTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the NB_IDLE_AFTER_TALK step: head-tracks the
